 "caveats": {
  "editorial_change": "Some change is editorial: O*NET rewrote 'and' as 'or' in many task statements, stripped vendor prefixes and generic suffixes from software names (about 7,000 renames across 2017-2024 releases), and moved to the O*NET-SOC 2010 and 2019 taxonomies. Matching rules fold these, but residual editorial change remains.",
  "national_data": "O*NET describes occupations nationally, not University positions.",
  "observed_usage_not_displacement": "AI usage exposure (Anthropic Economic Index) is observed Claude usage. It was published in 2025-2026, after every backtest origin, so it is used only as a clearly flagged ex-post feature. It is not a forecast of job loss.",
  "role_level_only": "Role-level evidence only: no person is read, stored or scored. Do not use for hiring, promotion, discipline, pay or any decision about an individual (Illinois HB 3773).",
  "rolling_updates": "O*NET updates occupations on a rolling schedule (each occupation's tasks are re-surveyed roughly every 5-10 years). Release-to-release change therefore mostly reflects WHEN an occupation was updated, not how fast the work changed. Indicators here are measured at real update events, and the timing of updates is modelled separately.",
  "technology_method": "Technology examples exist in the database files only from O*NET 21.0 (2016). From about 2018 O*NET adds software examples from job-posting data in bulk, so technology adoption partly reflects O*NET's collection method, not only employer adoption.",
  "unreviewed_mapping": "SUCSS classes are linked through the rank-1 candidate in sucss_mapping/outputs/candidates.parquet (review_status = unreviewed). Validate before use."
 },
